create_issue "Audit dashboard API contracts and OpenAPI coverage" "backend,shared-web,web-migration,priority:high" "M9 — Web Migration Discovery" $'Validate backend contracts used by both dashboards and make the migration gaps visible.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Every vendor and admin request is mapped to an endpoint\n- [ ] Request, response, pagination, filtering, and error shapes are documented\n- [ ] Missing or inaccurate OpenAPI definitions are listed\n- [ ] Upload and Stripe redirect contracts are documented\n- [ ] Contract gaps become linked follow-up issues'
create_issue "Define Next.js dashboard architecture and engineering conventions" "shared-web,web-migration,setup,priority:high" "M9 — Web Migration Discovery" $'Record the architectural decisions that both web dashboards will follow.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] App Router, rendering, caching, and client-component boundaries are defined\n- [ ] Workspace, package ownership, imports, and naming conventions are defined\n- [ ] TanStack Query, forms, validation, tables, charts, and uploads have standard patterns\n- [ ] Authentication and authorization boundaries are documented\n- [ ] Testing and deployment conventions are included'
create_issue "Define migration rollout, rollback, and parity sign-off process" "web-migration,devops,testing,priority:high" "M9 — Web Migration Discovery" $'Define how the web dashboards will run alongside Flutter and how parity will be approved.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- [ ] Staging, limited rollout, production cutover, and rollback stages are defined\n- [ ] Vendor and admin parity owners/checklists are defined\n- [ ] Data compatibility and backward compatibility requirements are documented\n- [ ] Legacy Flutter freeze and archive criteria are defined\n- [ ] Go/no-go checklist is agreed'

